    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on this September 21, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor, commanding an elite score of 81.88. His matchup against Trey Yesavage is our most favorable of the day, as the combination of a high-ceiling park environment and his optimal #3 spot in the order provides a perfect storm for production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** also profiles as a \"Strong\" start at 76.77; while his dynamic platoon split against the right-handed Shane Baz introduces minor friction, his current form and projected #2 slot make him a high-floor cornerstone for our Roto categories. We are also looking for **Coby Mayo** to provide secondary pop against Yesavage; he holds a 61.78 rating, with his aggressive 4th-spot positioning helping to mitigate the moderate threat posed by the opposing starter\u2019s xERA.\n\nThe decision to start **Nasim Nunez** at 50.27 remains purely a strategic play for speed, as our focus on the scarce SB category necessitates his presence despite a mediocre raw projection. He is currently our most marginal play, anchored by a #9 order position that limits his run-scoring opportunities. We are navigating a difficult day for depth, as the bench remains depleted by the inactive statuses of **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill** due to team off-days, compounded by the long-term IL designations for **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages**. With no viable candidates like **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, or **Heliot Ramos** active to shift into the lineup, we are proceeding with a restricted roster. Caution is advised for all active starters, as final lineup confirmations are still pending; any shift in order for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Gunnar Henderson** could necessitate a recalibration of our expected output for the evening.",
